tion/gzip","state":"uploaded","size":8320831,"digest":"sha256:f527d1374765d826c1627ceab3d1f46e548268731a495b5b12a3af529b3d79e8","download_count":2665,"created_at":"2026-10-28T15:36:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T15:36:17Z"},{"id":685449356,"node_id":"RA_kwDOOBOm5M4o2yCM","name":"rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":111,"digest":"sha256:2556b7767e5ae641812793e075e25a26b77c304dd75070779c269c2d3e7b558a","download_count":42,"created_at":"2026-10-28T15:36:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T15:36:16Z"},{"id":685449350,"node_id":"RA_kwDOOBOm5M4o2yCG","name":"rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/gzip","state":"uploaded","size":8312028,"digest":"sha256:395c4061041c5a25301c7b3564a93c4a661ed4df93427a77b6fc9e426ec8a13a","download_count":1070,"created_at":"2026-10-28T15:36:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T15:36:17Z"},{"id":685449364,"node_id":"RA_kwDOOBOm5M4o2yCU","name":"rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":112,"digest":"sha256:9d3a04059c4e413cd9e1b34fc4b9bd6669c701ac4f947dcb35816a508f966b4e","download_count":748,"created_at":"2026-10-28T15:36:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T15:36:16Z"}],"body":"\n### Fixed\n\n- Upgrade pulldown-cmark to fix exponential parser event growth and duplicate\n  diagnostics after empty wikilink labels (RUSTSEC-2026-0414), and upgrade Tokio\n  to address its I/O safety advisory (RUSTSEC-2026-0386). Release publication now\n  requires a fresh dependency security audit, including during recovery runs.\n- MD087 recognizes inline suppression of heading-capitalization diagnostics,\n  avoiding false unused-disable warnings (#973).\n- MD022 enforces configured spacing below headings before lists and code fences,\n  including when MD031 or MD032 is disabled. Overlapping spacing fixes insert\n  the required blank lines only once (#971).\n- MD067 can safely reorder complete footnote definitions to match their first\n  references. Reordering is atomic, preserves surrounding content and directive\n  scope, and leaves ambiguous Markdown or MDX cases report-only (#969).\n- MD013 recognizes additional common abbreviations and titles, including numeric\n  references with formatted numbers, while preserving sentence boundaries after\n  ambiguous units and labels. Sentence-spacing checks share this behavior (#966).\n- MD013 preserves meaningful indentation inside multiline code spans following\n  a bare list marker when reflowing text.\n\n- **security**: patch parser dependencies and gate release publication ([41d60e1](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/commit/41d60e1ff6701c2c80ae515f7994b19793bbae80))\n- **ci**: install only the tools required by parity checks ([ce014aa](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/commit/ce014aab5cb71ae44327058a50972030c0555a88))\n- **MD013**: preserve code-span indentation after bare list markers ([9cf648f](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/commit/9cf648ff2d1bbaf0f8f118377810876a77dbbcef))\n\n\n## Downloads\n\n| File | Platform | Checksum |\n|------|----------|----------|\n| [rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz) | Linux x86_64 | [checksum](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz.sha256) |\n| [rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz) | Linux x86_64 (musl) | [checksum](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz.sha256) |\n| [rumdl-v0.3.2-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz) | Linux ARM64 | [checksum](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz.sha256) |\n| [rumdl-v0.3.2-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz) | Linux ARM64 (musl) | [checksum](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz.sha256) |\n| [rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz) | macOS x86_64 | [checksum](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz.sha256) |\n| [rumdl-v0.3.2-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz) | macOS ARM64 (Apple Silicon) | [checksum](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz.sha256) |\n| [rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip) | Windows x86_64 | [checksum](https://github.com/rvben/rumdl/releases/download/v0.3.2/rumdl-v0.3.2-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip.sha256) |\n\n## Installation\n\n### Using uv (Recommended)\n```bash\nuv tool install rumdl\n```\n\n### Using pip\n```bash\npip install rumdl\n```\n\n### Using pipx\n```bash\npipx install rumdl\n```\n\n### Direct Download\nDownload the appropriate binary for your platform from the table above, extract it, and add it to your PATH.\n"}
